The six launcher scripts now select only modern 64-bit build outputs.

Set JIP_BUILD_DIR to the directory containing the rebuilt executables if it is
not one of the nearby build/cmake, build/arm64, or build directories.
Arguments and paths containing spaces are preserved. Archived Darwin/i686/Cygwin
executables are never selected as a fallback. JIP_HOME may still be used by the
tools for documentation lookup; it no longer controls binary selection here.

Use the CMake build instructions in ../documentation/64bit-repair-2.md.
